# Architecture Patterns

## Feature-First Structure

New features go under `lib/features/<feature_name>/` with this layout:

```
lib/features/my_feature/
  presentation/
    screens/       # full-page widgets (Screens)
    widgets/       # reusable feature-scoped widgets
  data/            # repositories, API mappers (optional)
  domain/          # models, interfaces (optional)
```

Shared widgets used across features belong in `lib/widgets/`.

## Routing (GoRouter)

All routes are declared in `lib/app.dart`.

- Navigate imperatively: `context.go('/customers')` or `context.push('/customers/new')`.
- Pass params via path (`':id'`) or query string (`state.uri.queryParameters`).
- **Protected routes**: `/dashboard`, `/customers`, `/workouts`, `/profile`, `/settings`, `/exercise-library` all require an authenticated Supabase user. The global `redirect` guard in `_goRouter` handles this automatically.
- When adding a new protected route, add its path prefix to the `isProtectedRoute` check in `lib/app.dart`.

## Dependency Injection (get_it)

```dart
// Register (in service_locator.dart)
getIt.registerLazySingleton<MyService>(() => MyService());

// Resolve (anywhere)
final service = getIt<MyService>();
```

Never instantiate services directly inside widgets or screens — always resolve from `getIt`.

## Supabase Auth

```dart
// Current user
final user = Supabase.instance.client.auth.currentUser;

// Bearer token for GymBlog.API (injected by GymBlogApiClient interceptor)
final token = Supabase.instance.client.auth.currentSession?.accessToken;
```

## Offline-First Write Path

1. Write mutations to `PendingOperations` outbox via `OfflineLocalStore`.
2. Optimistically update `LocalEntities` cache.
3. `SyncOrchestrator` replays the outbox when online / on auth change / on app resume.
4. Conflicts land in `PendingOpRow.conflictRemoteJson` for manual resolution.

Never call the remote API directly from a screen for write operations — go through the offline store so changes survive connectivity loss.
